          "body": {
            "hinglish": "Inheritance mein child class parent ke fields aur methods ko dobara likhe bina use karti hai, aur apna bhi kuch jod sakti hai. extends keyword se inheritance hota hai. Single, multilevel aur hierarchical inheritance Java mein hote hain, multiple inheritance class se nahi hota. Method overriding mein child parent ke method ko apne hisaab se dobara likhta hai, aur @Override likhna achhi aadat hai. private field child ko nahi milta, protected milta hai. Agle article mein hum Polymorphism seekhenge — ek hi naam, kai roop.",
            "english": "In inheritance, a child class uses the fields and methods of the parent without writing them again, and it can also add something of its own. Inheritance happens with the extends keyword. Single, multilevel and hierarchical inheritance happen in Java, multiple inheritance does not happen through a class. In method overriding, the child writes the method of the parent again in its own way, and writing @Override is a good habit. A private field does not come to the child, a protected field does. In the next article we will learn Polymorphism — one name, many forms.",
            "hindi": "Inheritance में child class parent के fields और methods को दोबारा लिखे बिना इस्तेमाल करती है, और अपना भी कुछ जोड़ सकती है। extends keyword से inheritance होता है। Single, multilevel और hierarchical inheritance जावा में होते हैं, multiple inheritance class से नहीं होता। Method overriding में child parent के method को अपने हिसाब से दोबारा लिखता है, और @Override लिखना अच्छी आदत है। private field child को नहीं मिलता, protected मिलता है। अगले article में हम Polymorphism सीखेंगे — एक ही नाम, कई रूप।"
          }
